The Factory is not the guardrail itself.
It is responsible for:

Creating and orchestrating the appropriate guardrails.
This separation is also consistent with modern guardrail systems: input checks, output checks, and tool checks happen at different workflow boundaries rather than one giant check at the end.
And for a banking system, tool/action guardrails are especially important because an agent that can actually perform account or transaction operations needs authorization and parameter checks before execution.

